            <ArticleTitle>Natural history of distal spinal agenesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the natural course in patients with distal spinal agenesis (DSA). Specifically, we compared children with different types of DSA (Renshaw sacral agenesis types I-IV) and determined their maximum ambulatory abilities, identified patients at risk for decubiti, determined the average number of operations per patient, described associated congenital anomalies, and sought a correlation between different types of DSA and the risk of back pain and development of scoliosis. Through a retrospective analysis, we concluded that there are definite correlations between the specific type DSA and the natural course with regard to all these entities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
